    "created_at": "2016-11-19T11:45:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-19T11:45:26Z",
    "body": "@domenic You're right: telling UAs should warn for caps lock on password field (like Windows does when login in Seven) would cover more than 80% of the use case with way fewer efforts than adding the new attribute.\n@annevk \n1 - Fields are case sensitive, but server-side code sometimes is not (usernames are usually case insensitive, but I also saw some websites having case-insensitive passwords...).\n2 - There is this snippet http://www.codeproject.com/Articles/17180/Detect-Caps-Lock-with-Javascript and that longer article http://www.4guysfromrolla.com/articles/051408-1.aspx (leading to the same JS code). They guess the caps lock status by analyzing the key pressed.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
