    "created_at": "2016-11-19T16:35:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-19T16:35:40Z",
    "body": "So you won't add \"UA should show user a warning if the input device is in upper or lower case lock.\" even on `type=password` ( https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#password-state-(type=password) )? You may close this then.\nBut there is a \"The user agent should obscure the value so that people other than the user cannot see it.\" condition, so having \"Therefore, UA should show user a warning if the input device is in upper case lock.\" could make sense (practically, it's because implementations does not follow \"people other than the user cannot see it\", but more \"people including the user cannot see it\").\n\nOne way another, yes, I'll keep track of this issue on each browser's issue tracking. It only sounds more standard to me if it was spec-agreed.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
